  "notes": "USAGE:\nOriginally a military term meaning to drive back an attacking force. In modern everyday use, also commonly applied to repelling pests, burglars, or other unwanted things. The pattern 〜を{撃退|げきたい}する is standard.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {敵|てき}を{撃退|げきたい}する: to repel the enemy\n- {害虫|がいちゅう}{撃退|げきたい}: pest repelling\n- {不審者|ふしんしゃ}を{撃退|げきたい}する: to drive off a suspicious person\n- {撃退|げきたい}に{成功|せいこう}する: to succeed in repelling",
